WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.970
When it becomes okay

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.960
to, you know, damage people's properties

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.200
and wake them up in the middle of the night

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.650
when terror is seen as

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.969
justified i think it's inevitable that

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:13.559
something terrible

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.000
is going to happen.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.300
On Saturday, August 29, 2020,

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.910
a pro-Trump demonstrator was shot and killed

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.380
during ongoing street protests in Portland.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.369
Last week, I interviewed, veteran journalist
Nancy Rommelmann,

00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:27.650
who has covered the Portland protests for
Reason

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.880
and has talked to dozens of demonstrators,

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.079
trying to understand their mindsets and motivations.

00:00:33.079 --> 00:00:35.390
She worries that as the protest movement continues,

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:38.739
it’s becoming increasingly restive, unfocused,

00:00:38.739 --> 00:00:41.320
and headed into dangerous territory.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.399
We go into 2020, which is obviously going
to

00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:44.399
be an election year,

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.900
then Covid hits, businesses close, and

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.080
the city

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.620
closed, and downtown became kind of

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:50.400
barren.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.879
The schools are closed,

00:00:51.879 --> 00:00:53.719
and everybody's home including tons and

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:54.780
tons of young people.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.620
And then George Floyd is killed and the

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:59.140
the city explodes.

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:00.880
For a very long time, they were peaceful

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:01.890
protests.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:02.890
You know moms and kids and

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:04.870
the line of cars that go around.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:05.870
'Toot-toot!.'

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:06.870
But,

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:07.880
per usual, these things you've got a

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:09.830
small contingent that wants to

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:10.830
fuck shit up.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:11.880
They showed up down at

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:12.880
Justice Center.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.110
They broke the windows.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:15.310
They threw furniture around.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:16.310
They set a

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:17.310
fire.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.310
I wrote a piece for Reason about

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:19.310
a woman that was trapped in the basement.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:20.310
The problem is

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.070
the mayor and the city council basically

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:23.070
just said

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:25.210
'you're not going to arrest peaceful

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.210
protesters.'

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.210
They stand they keep

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.210
committing violence

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:29.820
against the Justice Center and also next

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.200
door, which is the Federal Building

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.170
in late July, a special response team

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:35.080
from U.S Customs and Border Patrol

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.690
showed up in tactical gear ostensibly to

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:39.390
protect federal property.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.130
There were many bloody confrontations in

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:44.450
which protesters were tear gassed,

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:46.360
and some were caught on camera being

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.750
pulled into unmarked vans.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.460
Nobody wants to be tear gassed but

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.560
you've been pelting the building with

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:56.130
flaming trash for three hours provoking

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.130
a reaction.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.130
They are still

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.110
calling this free speech but they're

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:01.530
terrorizing citizens

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:04.240
and they march to the nearest place that

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.240
they

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:07.840
feel must be overtaken: police stations,

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:08.840
police unions,

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:11.060
a social services building, ICE

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:12.080
headquarters.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.040
They trash it, they set fire to it, and

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.900
they go into the residential streets.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.340
Now they're shining lights into people's

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.180
windows and saying,

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:20.180
"Get up motherfucker!

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.180
Get up.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.180
I'm out here

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:23.219
every night, fighting for change

00:02:23.219 --> 00:02:24.920
and we want you to know that and we want

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:26.750
you to be uncomfortable."

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.739
Some of these people are 20 years old

00:02:28.739 --> 00:02:30.650
and I have said to them, you know,

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.940
what is it that you want, and it's like

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.620
'Defund the police!'

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.460
It's like, okay,

00:02:37.469 --> 00:02:39.090
all right so then where do we go from

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:40.090
there.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.579
I was at a march

00:02:41.579 --> 00:02:45.379
where the police remained entirely passive, entirely.

00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:46.379
They finally came

00:02:46.379 --> 00:02:47.510
out because their union was being burnt

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:48.510
down for the that burnt down.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:49.510
There was a

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:50.510
fire there.

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:51.510
They were

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.590
pelting it for the umpteenth time.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:53.590
They finally just

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.700
stood there all the protesters like

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:57.459
got this close in their faces and then

00:02:57.459 --> 00:02:59.170
they just turned around and left.

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:02.659
That was by order of Ted Wheeler.

00:03:02.659 --> 00:03:05.310
I understand this idea they're trying to

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:06.310
provoke us.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:07.310
If we

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:09.530
don't be provoked maybe it dies down.

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:11.530
But there's too much momentum.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.730
And if it stays this hot i think it's

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:15.109
inevitable that something

00:03:15.109 --> 00:03:17.580
terrible is going to happen.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:19.580
And then whatever

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:20.080
side that terrible thing happens to

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.519
uses

00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:26.170
to say, 'look now we're justified in doing x.'

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:28.829
If you're a 22-year-old, and you're home,

00:03:28.829 --> 00:03:29.950
and you're not in school anymore, and

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.300
maybe your job has gone away because a

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.379
lot of jobs were lost in Portland,

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:36.129
you really are lost, and you are maybe

00:03:36.129 --> 00:03:37.761
lost for identity, and maybe you're

00:03:37.761 --> 00:03:39.090
looking for identity, and you're looking

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:40.659
for people to hang out with,

00:03:40.659 --> 00:03:42.629
and then you find it, and then you put on

00:03:42.629 --> 00:03:43.969
a, you know, an

00:03:43.969 --> 00:03:45.969
outfit, and you go out every night, and

00:03:45.969 --> 00:03:47.939
you feel energized, and I've had people

00:03:47.939 --> 00:03:49.480
tell me this it's like

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:52.090
it really is an incredible feeling of

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:53.715
being part of something

00:03:53.715 --> 00:03:54.560
Rommelmann worries that

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:55.889
a moral blindness

00:03:55.889 --> 00:03:58.230
is overtaking the protesters.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:00.239
I think that when

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:03.569
the definition of free speech or

00:04:03.569 --> 00:04:05.569
peaceful protest starts to become very

00:04:05.569 --> 00:04:07.249
elastic—when terror

00:04:07.249 --> 00:04:09.750
is seen as justified, we've seen how

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.269
these things go

00:04:11.269 --> 00:04:13.060
and they blame white supremacists of

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.409
Portland, or the city government, or the

00:04:14.409 --> 00:04:15.409
cops

00:04:15.409 --> 00:04:18.160
and they see what they're doing as

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:19.590
creating some sort of justice.

